DIRECT MOCK ACTION DRIVER
`DirectMissionDriver` in src/mission_manager/test/test_mission_ros_adapter.py calls the same
MissionActionAdapter admission/execute/cancel boundary used by ros_node.py. FakeChildClient drives
wait_for_server, send_goal(done_cb), bounded wait polling, server connectivity, terminal callbacks,
late callbacks, and cancel_goal without importing ROS. FakeScanBackend drives `.active` creation,
finalization metadata, startup failure, and cleanup.

FAILURE / BEHAVIOR MATRIX
- navigate success: one correlated move_base terminal -> OK.
- inspect + return: outbound navigation, validated scan, fresh directed return -> OK + .bag artifact.
- record_route + return: one recording brackets both directions -> OK + one finalized artifact.
- one active mission: second admission -> BUSY; active goal remains owner.
- malformed/unknown destination or mission type -> INVALID_GOAL before child dispatch.
- correlation: stale callback from prior generation ignored; current abort remains NAVIGATION_FAILED.
- child disconnect: unavailable move_base/server connectivity -> COMMUNICATION_LOST.
- shared stair/floor clients: coherent generated-interface-equivalent results cross both adapters once -> OK.
- stair child abort -> STAIR_FAILED; floor transition not dispatched.
- per-segment cancellation: only active move_base goal cancelled once -> CANCELLED/MISSION_ABORT; anchor remains home.
- empty scan metadata -> SCAN_FAILED; return not dispatched; no `.active` remains.
- rosbag start failure -> SCAN_FAILED; no `.active` remains.
- failed return (two move_base aborts) -> NAVIGATION_FAILED; successfully reached outbound anchor remains committed.
- confirmed anchors: only SegmentExecution.SUCCESS invokes Todo 7 LogicalAnchor.after_segment.

